# Public site origin.
#
# Every absolute URL the site emits is built from this: metadataBase, canonical
# tags, Open Graph / Twitter image URLs, sitemap.xml entries, robots.txt and the
# JSON-LD structured data.
#
# You normally do NOT need to set this. src/lib/site.ts falls back to the live
# production host (https://vedik-demo.netlify.app) when the variable is absent,
# so the deployed canonical URLs are correct out of the box.
#
# Set it in Netlify (Site settings > Environment variables) only when deploying
# a preview branch or a custom domain. Never point it at localhost in
# production: a localhost origin tells search engines to canonicalise the whole
# site to http://localhost:3000 and ignore it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://vedik-demo.netlify.app

# Only needed if the demo is served from a sub-path rather than a domain root.
# Keep in sync with NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL; see next.config.ts.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH=
